1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,826
More than one in four older adults fall each year, and less

2
00:00:03,826 --> 00:00:06,814
than half tell their doctor, according to the CDC.

3
00:00:06,814 --> 00:00:10,997
When a parent takes many medicines, a new side effect is easy to miss.

4
00:00:11,774 --> 00:00:14,587
Kinwise helps families notice those changes.

5
00:00:14,587 --> 00:00:18,935
Meet Margaret, seventy-eight, and her daughter Alex, both fictional.

6
00:00:19,709 --> 00:00:22,260
Margaret describes her day in her own words.

7
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:25,158
A clinical language engine reads it on her device.

8
00:00:25,930 --> 00:00:29,036
Woozy becomes dizziness, nearly went over becomes a

9
00:00:29,036 --> 00:00:31,716
near-fall, and no ankle swelling stays a no.

10
00:00:31,716 --> 00:00:35,188
My granddaughter Sofia fell is set aside as someone else.

11
00:00:35,188 --> 00:00:38,599
Margaret confirms every answer before anything is saved.

12
00:00:39,369 --> 00:00:40,550
Now Alex signs in.

13
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:44,421
Since lorazepam was started, dizziness was recorded on 9 of

14
00:00:44,421 --> 00:00:47,505
14 answered days, compared with 2 of 19 before.

15
00:00:47,505 --> 00:00:51,376
One fall and two near-falls were recorded on those 14 days.

16
00:00:51,376 --> 00:00:55,247
It shows a change in what was recorded, not what caused it.

17
00:00:56,018 --> 00:00:59,530
The timeline compares answered days before and after, with

18
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:01,830
Fisher's exact and Mann-Whitney tests.

19
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:05,887
Falls are listed by date, because a few events are too few to test.

20
00:01:06,658 --> 00:01:10,946
The review checks her eight medicines against AGS Beers 2023, the

21
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:15,894
anticholinergic burden scale, where her list adds up to 7, fall-risk lists,

22
00:01:15,894 --> 00:01:20,777
and prescribing cascades, like furosemide started for ankle swelling after

23
00:01:20,777 --> 00:01:21,502
amlodipine.

24
00:01:21,502 --> 00:01:26,648
Each finding ends in a question for her doctor or pharmacist, with its source.

25
00:01:27,421 --> 00:01:31,660
Before adding a medicine, Alex sees what would change: Advil PM would

26
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:35,162
add three review prompts, including a second product with

27
00:01:35,162 --> 00:01:36,145
diphenhydramine.

28
00:01:36,145 --> 00:01:38,664
Nothing is saved until Alex chooses Save.

29
00:01:39,541 --> 00:01:43,148
Ask Kinwise answers from the records: near-falls on 2 of 14

30
00:01:43,148 --> 00:01:45,470
answered days since lorazepam started.

31
00:01:45,470 --> 00:01:50,421
The optional on-device model, running on this laptop's GPU, adds a plainer draft.

32
00:01:50,421 --> 00:01:54,272
Code checks its numbers and medicine names against the records.

33
00:01:54,272 --> 00:01:58,122
A treatment question is redirected to her doctor or pharmacist.

34
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:01,630
The visit brief puts it on one page.

35
00:02:01,630 --> 00:02:06,120
Alex must mark it reviewed before it prints, and it exports

36
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:09,317
as an HL7 FHIR R4 bundle of 270 resources.

37
00:02:10,901 --> 00:02:16,719
Anyone can rerun both test suites in the browser: 94.2 percent micro-F1 on

38
00:02:16,719 --> 00:02:22,693
70 held-out diary stories, and 57 of 57 medication-review test cases passed.

39
00:02:23,464 --> 00:02:27,026
All safety logic is deterministic code with cited sources;

40
00:02:27,026 --> 00:02:28,930
the model only handles wording.

41
00:02:28,930 --> 00:02:30,711
Records stay in this browser.

42
00:02:31,484 --> 00:02:36,339
Working today: check-in, timeline, review, visit brief and FHIR export.

43
00:02:36,339 --> 00:02:40,441
Planned: a validation study with pharmacists and caregivers,

44
00:02:40,441 --> 00:02:42,903
pharmacy import, and family sharing.

45
00:02:42,903 --> 00:02:46,527
The knowledge base is not yet clinician-reviewed, and

46
00:02:46,527 --> 00:02:48,715
Kinwise gives no medical advice.

47
00:02:49,487 --> 00:02:49,991
Kinwise.

48
00:02:49,991 --> 00:02:53,516
Notice what changes after a medicine change, and bring a

49
00:02:53,516 --> 00:02:55,279
clear question to the visit.
